    "background_story": "In the ancient Persian Empire, Candy was a powerful satrap, or governor, of a vast province. Born into a noble family, she was educated in the arts of politics, diplomacy, and warfare. Candy's intelligence, strategic thinking, and charisma earned her the respect of the Emperor himself, who appointed her to govern the wealthy and influential province of Bactria. Under her wise and just rule, the province flourished, becoming a hub of trade, culture, and learning. Candy's fairness and compassion towards her subjects earned her their loyalty and admiration. She was known for her lavish patronage of the arts, and her court attracted scholars, poets, and musicians from all over the empire. Despite the challenges of ruling a vast and diverse territory, Candy remained a steadfast and effective leader, beloved by her people and respected by her peers.",
